1. The text argues that God creates all possibilities without judgment, and suffering exists because we choose subjective experiences that include it. It claims that our awareness of evil and suffering is a personal choice, not an objective reality forced upon us. Ultimately, we have agency to change our perspective or situation, even if we feel trapped.

2. I partially agree that perspective shapes experience, but I disagree that suffering is merely a choice. Many forms of suffering—like disease, abuse, or systemic oppression—are imposed on people without their consent or awareness, making the claim of full agency unrealistic and potentially dismissive of real harm.

3. God made all, both light and dark,  
A vast machine without a mark.  
We choose the lens through which we see—  
The pain we hold, the world we flee.  
Yet some are bound by chains unseen,  
Not choice, but weight of what has been. [end of text]


